 tute of Criminology\nTopics: Law\, Rights & Justice\, Criminology\nDetails
 : https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273143/\nSign-up needed\nThis event i
 s part of the Institute of Criminology's Public Guest Seminar Series for M
 ichaelmas Term 2026. A drinks reception follows the talk. These events are
  free and everyone is welcome. Please register to attend either in-person 
 or online by clicking the link at the bottom of this page. \n About What m
 ight it mean to live a flourishing life? And what is the relationship betw
 een flourishing and the virtues\, especially justice? In this talk based o
 n her recent book\, Professor Angie Hobbs explores how Plato can help us w
 ith these urgent questions\, and how he addresses the key issue of charact
 er formation\, and why it never benefits us to return wrong for wrong. She
  shows how she has used his methodology\, ideas and arguments in a variety
  of sectors to address contemporary issues in education\, faith–secular 
 debate\, health care and the civil service\, and invites the audience to d
 iscuss with
END:VEVENT
